{
  "_comment": [
    "Pinned MSYS2 toolchain for the Windows installer/helper builds.",
    "",
    "Why: the published Windows binaries are unsigned PEs whose AV verdict is",
    "per-hash (issue #157), so the bytes that CI ships must be the bytes a",
    "developer can rebuild.  msys2/setup-msys2 with update:false only skips",
    "pacman -Syu — it still installs whatever versions the runner's package DB",
    "offers, so binutils/crt/headers floated under a fixed gcc version and local",
    "builds diverged by ~4 KB of code from the CI artifact (see",
    "docs/DEVELOPING.md -> Why a clean local scan does not clear a CI build).",
    "This file pins the WHOLE package set: .github/actions/pinned-msys2 installs",
    "exactly these versions on the runner (pacman -U after the bootstrap, then",
    "verified), and `pnpm toolchain:local` extracts the same files into a",
    "project-local prefix so a local build can reproduce the shipped bytes.",
    "",
    "capturedFrom: the package set msys2/setup-msys2 installed in GitHub Actions",
    "run 34935654811 (2026-09-15, windows-latest) — the run whose Windows",
    "binaries VirusTotal flagged.  It is the best available starting point, not",
    "a reconstruction of that artifact: building its commit from this set gives",
    "binaries with a 2,752-byte-larger .text and one extra CRT import, because",
    "the run recorded installed versions but never recorded which compiler",
    "actually built them.  From the next publish on, every run logs the compiler",
    "and linker it used (`--provenance`), so this cannot recur silently.",
    "",
    "Refresh with `node tools/ci/msys2Toolchain.mjs --fetch --print-manifest`",
    "after a deliberate toolchain bump, then confirm the deterministic publish",
    "job's environment-vs-prefix comparison still passes and re-verify the",
    "AV/VT gates on the result."
  ],
  "capturedFrom": "gh run 34935654811 (2026-09-15, windows-latest)",
